    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The full verb «sein» and negation",
     "texto": [
      "**Nicht** negates a word or a whole idea. Its position depends on what we want to negate; there is no general rule to always put it after the verb. In these sentences it comes before the origin phrase: **Ich bin nicht aus Berlin** (I am not from Berlin), **Sie kommt nicht aus Deutschland** (she does not come from Germany).",
      "Look at **sie**: with a singular verb it means «she» (**sie ist**), and with a plural verb it means «they» (**sie sind**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
